Covers came from three tiers because each one genuinely failed for a chunk of the list: Open Library's ISBN-keyed covers API missed ~35% of the 141 books (small/regional publishers, or the CSV's ISBN pointing to an edition with no cover uploaded); stripping the trailing series marker (e.g. '(Harry Potter, #2)') before an Open Library title+author search recovered 13 of those, since OL's search doesn't fuzzy-match well with it present. For the rest, Google Books' unauthenticated API was tried first but hit a persistent 429 that didn't clear even after backoff/retries or a wait, so it was dropped entirely (see fetch-book-covers.py, kept untracked at the repo root). The final fallback used the Apify 'epctex/goodreads-scraper' actor — but only after confirming the hard way that its search-based input (both a /search?q= startUrl and its own 'search' field) silently returns zero items even on a successful request; only a direct /book/show/{id} URL actually gets parsed. The fix was to build that URL from the Goodreads CSV's own 'Book Id' column rather than searching at all, which resolved all 24 remaining books in one batch run.
